\title{Degenerate and non-degenerate bilinear forms}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{#{\operatorname{Ker}\phi_L} is the “left kernel of #{\phi}” and #{\operatorname{Ker}\phi_R} is the “right kernel of #{\phi}”. We say that #{\phi} is \em{non-degenerate} if}

##{\operatorname{Ker}\phi_L = \lbrace 0\rbrace  \text{ and } \operatorname{Ker}\phi_R = \lbrace 0\rbrace .}

\p{Otherwise, we say that #{\phi} is \em{degenerate}.}
